Wire hotset_protect into the upstream cache_ext policy build

The cache_ext clone at spike/ebpf_pagecache/cache_ext_upstream/ is kept
pristine (gitignored nested repo, same convention as spike/seismic_upstream).
This is the only change the hotset_protect spike needs inside their tree.

Their policies/Makefile already carries generic pattern rules that cover any
new policy:

    %.bpf.o : %.bpf.c $(VMLINUX_H) dir_watcher.bpf.h
    %.skel.h: %.bpf.o  $(VMLINUX_H)
    %.out   : %.c      %.skel.h

so the only edit required is adding hotset_protect.out to the `all` target.

APPLY (on the cache_ext kernel, after `./install_kernel.sh` and a reboot):

    SPIKE=/path/to/sfu-library-thinclient/spike/ebpf_pagecache
    cd "$SPIKE/cache_ext_upstream"
    cp "$SPIKE/hotset_protect.bpf.c" "$SPIKE/hotset_protect.c" policies/
    git apply "$SPIKE/cache_ext_hotset.patch"
    ./build_policies.sh          # -> policies/hotset_protect.out

REVERT:

    cd "$SPIKE/cache_ext_upstream"
    git apply -R "$SPIKE/cache_ext_hotset.patch"
    rm -f policies/hotset_protect.bpf.c policies/hotset_protect.c \
          policies/hotset_protect.bpf.o policies/hotset_protect.skel.h \
          policies/hotset_protect.out

(The copied sources and all build products are already covered by
policies/.gitignore for *.o/*.out/*.skel.h; the two .c files are not, so
remove them explicitly if you want `git status` clean in the nested repo.)

--- a/policies/Makefile
+++ b/policies/Makefile
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@

 all: 	cache_ext_mru.out cache_ext_mglru.out cache_ext_fifo.out \
 		cache_ext_sampling.out cache_ext_get_scan.out cache_ext_s3fifo.out \
-		cache_ext_lhd.out   \
+		cache_ext_lhd.out hotset_protect.out  \
 		# cache_ext_debug.out cache_ext_simple.out

 $(VMLINUX_H):
